# Runtime configuration.
#
# config/config.example.js tells the operator to copy it to config/config.local.js and fill in
# real Power Automate HTTP-trigger URLs, and states that "config/config.local.js is git-ignored
# — never commit real URLs". No .gitignore existed in this repository, so that protection was
# documented but not implemented: on a public repository a `git add .` after following those
# instructions would have published live endpoint URLs. Each such URL carries its own SAS
# signature and is, in the example file's own words, "effectively a credential".
config/config.local.js

# Generated tree snapshots. internalplatform.snapshot.json was a serialised copy of the very
# tree git already versions (163 files, none of them unique to it), regenerated and re-pinned
# by hand as the workstream moved. Git is the snapshot; a second one in the tree only drifts.
internalplatform.snapshot.json
internalplatform.baseline.json
*.snapshot.json

# Review/design bundles. These arrive as archives from the design tool, are not part of the
# runtime, and are not referenced by any module. One of them shipped three live Power Automate
# SAS URLs into this public repository; see the audit notes on the removal commit.
*.zip

# Local tooling and OS noise.
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
